  },
  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "Playing the Game",
    "section": "1.99",
    "heading": "Order of Application",
    "lineStart": 779,
    "lineEnd": 783
  },
  "section": "1.99",
  "rulesText": "Modifiers to damage are applied in the following order: adjustments such as bonuses, penalties, or multipliers are applied first; Resistance is applied second; and Vulnerability is applied third.\n\nFor example, a creature has Resistance to all damage and Vulnerability to Fire damage, and it's within a magical aura that reduces all damage by 5. If it takes 28 Fire damage, the damage is first reduced by 5 (to 23), then halved for the creature's Resistance (and rounded down to 11), then doubled for its Vulnerability (to 22)."
}
